Several outlets quote the same Truth Social post from Thursday, Oct 15, 2026. CNBC, the Washington Times, Axios and The Hill all report it. In the post, Trump wrote: "If Ken Paxton loses, it will be because of WEAK and INEFFECTIVE Political Hacks like John Cornyn and Karl Rove" (
CNBC
; 
Washington Times
; 
Axios
). The Hill likewise reports that 
Trump called Cornyn and Rove "WEAK" and "INEFFECTIVE political hacks."
 The attribution, the target, the "fault" framing and the "weak and ineffective political hacks" wording all match the claim as worded. I did not find the post on Truth Social itself, but the quote is consistent across independent outlets.
